        "mission_intent": "We need a comprehensive Configuration Management Plan specification developed for the NEXUS-3 enclave, aligned with NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5 CM-9 requirements and referenced guidance in SP 800-128. The plan must clearly define roles, responsibilities, and the processes and procedures governing configuration management across all system components. It should establish a formal process for identifying configuration items throughout the entire system development life cycle, from initial design through decommission. Additionally, the plan needs to integrate our existing system component inventory practices under CM-8, specifically ensuring that every component is assigned to a designated system and that an acknowledgement of that assignment is received from the component owner or designated system administrator\u2014no unmanaged assets should exist outside this framework. Please coordinate with the Privacy Office where component tracking mechanisms could implicate individual privacy data. The deliverable should reference OMB A-130 and the SP 800-57 series for any cryptographic module inventory items. We need a draft ready for ISSO review by end of next quarter, with a final version briefed to the Authorizing Official within thirty days after that. Route the draft through the Change Control Board and include a crosswalk showing how each plan element traces back to the relevant control enhancements.",
